<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Andronikos Asen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1355</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Andronikos Palaiologos Asen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Andronikos Asen was a Byzantine aristocrat of Bulgarian royal descent who served as governor of the Byzantine province of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Morea</a>. In 1320 he captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karytaina">Karytaina</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akova">Akova</a> and other castles in the centre of the Peloponnese from the Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaea">Achaea</a>, ending Frankish rule there. He later held commands in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a>.</p></div>
